{
 "section_summary": "This section consists chiefly of records removed from the Japanese Legation in Panama and marked September 21, 1945. It contains the end of an unidentified Japanese statistical document, a Japanese Foreign Ministry manual on composing economical Romanized telegrams, and a large collection of prewar registration, passport, household and address records for Japanese residents of Panama and Colón. The resident records preserve names, birth and family details, occupations, Japanese home addresses, Panamanian addresses and older immigration or registration dates, although much of the OCR is severely damaged.",
