  {
   "title": "Japanese resident, passport and household registration records for Panama and Colón",
   "doc_type": "consular register and identification-card compilation",
   "start_page": 25,
   "end_page": 80,
   "continues_previous": false,
   "date": "1945-09-21",
   "from": "Japanese Legation, Panama",
   "to": "",
   "about": "A compilation of personal and household records for Japanese residents of Panama, especially Panama City and Colón.",
   "summary": "These pages reproduce numerous forms, cards and register entries recording Japanese names, birth dates, Japanese domiciles, occupations, parents, spouses, children, arrival or registration dates and street addresses in Panama. Many subjects lived in Colón or Panama City, while their registered origins range across Japanese prefectures including Shizuoka, Hiroshima, Yamaguchi, Kumamoto, Fukushima, Tokushima and Wakayama. Several cards also record movements to Venezuela or Caracas, and older entry stamps date chiefly from 1930-1940. The repeated English legend attributes the compilation to the Japanese Legation in Panama and dates its transfer or processing to September 21, 1945.",
